{"title":"2004 IMO Shortlist Problems/A2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/A2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(<i>Mihai Bălună, Romania</i>)\nAn infinite sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/c/61c1c1c657c50f64a117edc2dabca6dc5baa4ff9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0, a_1, a_2, \\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"95\" height=\"11\" /> of real numbers satisfies the condition\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/e/15e1768606b335e0f40613a292115e9a57bf2cd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n = | a_{n+1} - a_{n+2} | \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" /> for every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/c/e2c7d62172af0e738dd12f47f3f8ad8ef70cd65f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />,\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/5/ee5c7c921b3334f6ecf58c241eeea42acf0ce71e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> positive and distinct.  Can this sequence be bounded?\n</p><p><i>This was also Problem 4 of the 2005 German Pre-<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=TST\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"TST\">TST</a> and Problem 1 of the first 2005 black <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MOP\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"MOP\">MOP</a> test.  It was Problem 3, Day 2 of the 2005 Romanian TST in the following form:</i>\n</p><p>A sequence of real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/4/5745e048a216d85859c80beb6b69015d3ed41eb5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{a_n\\}_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"18\" /> is called a <i>bs</i> sequence if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/3/7b3cc10e9aafa734bad8d2df32a0242d47e461dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n = |a_{n+1} - a_{n+2}|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" />, for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/0/0f0d43e758d9cef0fe802a89ff590f52ee8d766f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />. Prove that a bs sequence is bounded if and only if the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> given by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51dccbb9f7a1fe3956b86491651e73d6f26cd6ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n,k)=a_na_k(a_n-a_k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"186\" height=\"18\" />, for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/3/d73445dadeda6d3b9f0a58e6d4f066ea4910408a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n,k\\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" /> is the null function.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/A2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/A2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We note that each of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> must be nonnegative.\n</p><p><b>Lemma 1.</b> If the two initial terms of the sequence are nonzero and distinct, then every term of the sequence is nonzero and no two consecutive terms are equal.\n</p><p><i>Proof.</i>  We proceed by induction; we are given a base case.  If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/4/cc468e5212d08ac227dd4000cc89d5729d3926d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${}a_k \\neq a_{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"17\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/0/250ed1ac8a3eefc2ef83cd63bc11aa921d2a4d9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$| a_{k+1} - a_{k+2} | \\neq a_{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"158\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/5/625de9b5599f386b44458b38ea9c3d7a15a5a95d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k+2} \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"17\" />.  Furthermore, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/9/2c93f7901045ce49c61553945619e273f767b7b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a_{k+1} - a_{k+2}| = a_k \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"176\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/d/81dd8eac4d191ec906a186dcdabbac9a90b2a886.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k+1} \\neq a_{k+2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"92\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Consider a sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/4/ab49b9013d949f799f0e6a4247e80c1fa181c59b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{b_i\\}_{i=0}^{\\infty}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" /> of positive reals which obeys the recursive relation\n</p>\n<center> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/0/eb054bb6a9e895398dc717d1cffc058d56a0cd44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{n+2} = |b_{n+1} - b_n |$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"138\" height=\"18\" />. </center>\n<p><b>Lemma 2.</b> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/8/2b842371229c761f1cd4bf1ca9bce436cd4af043.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\min (b_i, b_{i+1}, b_{i+2}) \\ge \\min (b_{i+3}, b_{i+4}, b_{i+5})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"308\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><i>Proof.</i>  We note that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/4/ec4ab0208929896d52a75f725d29af270afe9561.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_k \\le b_{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"16\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/d/c0dea488464422906f059e18471c404676d18a22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{k+2} = b_{k+1} - b_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6c585549e98cc9f625779466ee4ee1a6722045d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{k+3} = b_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" />.  Thus if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/1/6d1822a7f96e7d5ae9ecd113e64f8821f208a682.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{i+3}, b_{i+4}, b_{i+5} &gt; \\min(b_i, b_{i+1}, b_{i+2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"263\" height=\"18\" />, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/7/547fd52b4a201fb13f81e67477325b4932018556.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_i, b_{i+1} &gt; b_{i+2} &gt; b_{i+3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"158\" height=\"16\" />, a contradiction.\n</p><p><b>Lemma 3.</b> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/4/b24470c5feb30d835b9bc1a6dee1d3314a3be1a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = \\left\\lfloor \\frac{b_{k-1}}{b_k} \\right\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"86\" height=\"43\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/a/b2a3ba90b4af9721a479f28cea1a8fb1d23cb74c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j = \\left\\lceil \\frac{3}{2}r \\right\\rceil$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"71\" height=\"43\" />.  Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/4/2641b592b2c6cced8f6526b507f003158705140a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\min (b_{k+j},b_{k+j+1},b_{k+j+2}) \\le \\frac{1}{2}b_{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"259\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p><i>Proof.</i>  For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/9/4699a807d38bad28045195e4b10a61e4e10fa353.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2i+2 \\le r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"79\" height=\"15\" />, easy induction yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/e/82e35b78dfe3d0d95f306384d7310715d1082ff0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{k+3i} = b_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/c/afc5c1e09dad040e52af92ac5542a84f386ae153.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{k+3i+1} = b_{k-1} - (2i+1)b_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"212\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/1/8917471cd4a51362a511f54278fb16df81b9ef24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{k+3i+2} = b_{k-1} - (2i+2)b_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"209\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Now, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is even, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/4/5d41d673ece72f843edb3dbfab1a050891ca1eed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{k+3r/2 - 1} = b_{k-1} - b_kr$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"173\" height=\"18\" />, which is less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/b/b6bdec4394870e8a713538ce428bea9d41c8775f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> by the definition of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/d/76d70d51cedb79477744d21e55d354f796d1f129.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{k+3r/2} = b_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"92\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/e/7deaf006b567b69146c0ba84ea0acc93908c662d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{k+3r/2 +1} = b_{3r/2} - b_{k+3r/2-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"219\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/0/c10b9025d1a90c0b2b2b0d95fb544836e99bd470.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{k+3r/2+2} = b_{k+3r/2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"145\" height=\"18\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/1/04103af85105c63ad8168fdaa71aea05a7e2d9e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{k+3r/2+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/b/ecb0a2d5d202bedbf732bcf8f2d3361936b54f0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{k+3r/2+2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" /> add to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/600c602774ff5c52546a69c2c9ee788989b2b030.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{3r/2} = b_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" />, one of them must be at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/f/befeefe06b6c314c38811fc8fdb7fcedf273c013.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{b_k}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"18\" height=\"37\" />, and the lemma follows.\n</p><p>On the other hand, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is odd, then set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/3/a33bb15e8d817e04cbc72d610cd0b547eaf550f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s = r-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"75\" height=\"15\" /> and we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/f/2afad2848059c499dd4fe8fa87f49901f43c50d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{k+3s/2+1} = b_{k-1} - b_kr &lt; b_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"212\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/0/430ab1e4925132a916989a4c1533609e2036b78e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{k+3s/2 + 2} = b_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"108\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/f/7efa81dc780fd3c6ea426f84c2ac0dc7523a8453.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{k+3s/2+3} = b_{k+3s/2 + 2} - b_{k+3s/2+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"252\" height=\"18\" />, so as before, at least one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/0/5b0c6ae3a813e19b2a5fb7abf50836122c431a0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{k+3s/2+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/f/4df8fb199da81fa25ff26adc58fe954ab57d402d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{k+3s/2+3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /> must be at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/f/befeefe06b6c314c38811fc8fdb7fcedf273c013.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{b_k}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"18\" height=\"37\" />.  In fact, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/0/c609701b4aab1b110f06670dc076461d2de44176.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${} b_{k+3s/2+4}= b_{k+3s/2+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"160\" height=\"18\" />, so the minimum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/5/d25699dd620979ee913e1b52848e6201c4857773.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{k+3s/2+3}, b_{k+3s/2+4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"145\" height=\"18\" /> is at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/f/befeefe06b6c314c38811fc8fdb7fcedf273c013.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{b_k}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"18\" height=\"37\" />, upholding the lemma, since in this case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/e/fbed8231757fcdd030b778ecb709f962dff04be1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lceil \\frac{3}{2}r \\right\\rceil = \\frac{3}{2}s+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"119\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nNow, suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/3/8f3a12e55ba898ce77e8b3c18b2d54f9e563b551.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{ a_i \\}_{i=0}^{\\infty}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" /> is bounded, i.e., there exists some real <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> greater than each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />.  By setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/2/6b28857a17137b4f9f2e8bade57c8c292a42aacc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1, b_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"37\" height=\"16\" /> equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/a/f0ab39df6c21ae9087326d8ee522254e78468dd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n-1}, a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"11\" />, we generate the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> in reverse, and from Lemma 2, we can see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/d/1ad9d53a7fd10d8297ac042fcbe8c01dddacf36f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = \\min (a_1,a_2,a_3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"150\" height=\"18\" /> is a lower bound of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />.  But by making <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/0/a00f8c3c75c4cefb7407bab4c607b48c8328d1c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lceil \\log_2 (N/m) +1 \\rceil \\left\\lceil \\frac{3}{2} \\left\\lfloor \\frac{N}{m} \\right\\rfloor \\right\\rceil$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"216\" height=\"45\" />, by applying Lemma 3, we obtain the result <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/8/038f0976811491a5757b2cd7c9a938db803c5096.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\le \\frac{1}{2} m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"69\" height=\"37\" />, which is a contradiction when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/9/a0900cb9d24185bd920f9f30d5b669147a7ea47a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0, a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" /> are distinct and greater than 0, by Lemma 1.\n</p><p>Now, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/b/adbb4f5b218da0beb45e5303f1be33847b11bf01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_na_k(a_n-a_k) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"20\" /> for all natural <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, all the nonzero <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> must be equal and the sequence is bounded.  On the other hand, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/f/6af4bd6c2d8e7dc6cf76d98fd92ec124f3716ac0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n+1}a_n(a_{n+1}-a_n) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"177\" height=\"18\" /> always holds, then either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/f/b9f1a207b538acd864bab858c82e53360b46590b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n+1} = a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/c/e6ca45284ba5fdcf107581d9b38db58bdf1c1a78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n+2} = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"16\" />, or one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/f/9cfc958ef538abdf45b694a4c6fd319684a19938.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n+1}, a_{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" /> is equal to zero and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/b/bdbad7ba60dda501e6b1cd313ae3bf4090e8f981.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n+2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> is equal to the other one; hence by induction, all the nonzero terms of the sequence are equal, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/c/7ccd61a9535f30870f2292d5920e0448831714ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_na_k(a_n-a_k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"107\" height=\"18\" /> is always equal to zero.  Hence if for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/f/3cff91106986d596b444b21427ff9ee5ac08db4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n, k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/9/339f11de317df03365375d8e94f308fc66e6c2ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${} a_na_k(a_n-a_k) \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"142\" height=\"18\" />, then there exist two distinct positive consecutive terms of sequence, which is then unbounded as proven above.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/A2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The given recursive condition is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/e/abe1fedcd7ec6f8b23ada2a2bf131bc4dd97547a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n+2} = a_{n+1} + a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"138\" height=\"16\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/0/ef0dd6c4580adf0d511b7da50b8f530b79a27266.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n+1} &lt; a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/a/eea8fc5b7c0332ede29d720572c329a60c3c001c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n+2} = a_{n+1} \\pm a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"135\" height=\"16\" /> otherwise. Note that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/e/67e2dcf8777e4ef100fbc0532484f177db7d3483.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n+1} &gt; a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/4/b34d0793c32b89f047033a709c9beae3ca59dcf5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n+1} = a_n + a_{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"134\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p><b>Lemma 1: </b> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/4/1d4f05dbfb8deab8d418a36643fded9383c604eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" /> be the minimal element of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/d/cad681354a2a529a1828a56b2b5629faec3cd128.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{a_n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/5/585d501a64a47152ab58f71726e1b91753c3e2f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = \\text{min}\\,(a_0,a_1,a_2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"151\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><i>Proof: </i> Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5bb76208dae30e44513fa10ff49ba1329094713.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\ge 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" /> is the minimal value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/3/1e30377bf3609e647cca4d3cf5ce883ffa41086d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"10\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/7/d679083312e17381307ace07bdd5b0e9ca303fc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k = a_{k-1} - a_{k-2} \\Longrightarrow a_{k-1} &gt; a_{k-2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"265\" height=\"12\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb89ceeb3ff79d04673bf1cf3074ed501b6fad6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k-1} = a_{k-2} + a_{k-3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"149\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/7/737728c9b5deb36fbfabae47090907d25ad7e879.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k = a_{k-3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"75\" height=\"10\" />. This contradicts our assumption of minimality. \n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/f/d6f5965a80d91aa7dcc7b7a91f03e0f04873b92a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_n = a_n + a_{n+1} + a_{n+2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"176\" height=\"16\" />; we claim that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/0/210b766e365514dc8beb1dcc9426fa2980a13007.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_{n+2} &gt; T_n + m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"118\" height=\"16\" />, which would imply that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/f/82f4341a1efbe1a890de160de023b4e4b84ef444.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> is unbounded, in turn implying that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1a2b6b7c193f9ba2b2134a59f1da5addcfbc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> is unbounded.\n</p>\n<ul><li>Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/3/cc3002f286d11ace031e787b2297e9c90768aa54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n+2} = a_n + a_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"133\" height=\"14\" />; then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/c/d6c129c1dc2d5459bffdc97b5d1e64066c5a38f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n+3} = a_{n+2} - a_{n+1} = a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"194\" height=\"12\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/4/d94620bba29aad13418366ea8631019991e3bce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n+3} = a_{n+2} + a_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"150\" height=\"14\" />. In the former case, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/6/8264dd1c775c3caf6019d685d9f5e2a99afb858e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n+3} &lt; a_{n+2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"14\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/1/101e99385a7af00af4aceb95e350f04ecf2e2219.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n+4} = a_{n+3} + a_{n+2} = a_n + a_{n+2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"255\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/2/1b2fbf53f2581765b4f6d878ec432b00f38f8381.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_{n+2} = (a_{n+2}) + (a_{n}) + (a_{n} + a_{n+2}) = T_n + 2a_n &gt; T_n + m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"453\" height=\"18\" />. In the latter case, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/2/4d23117acc7dbfb825bb4d439462eac248ba25bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_{n+2} &gt; a_{n+2} + a_{n+3} + m &gt; T_n + a_{n+1} + m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"331\" height=\"16\" />.</li>\n<li>Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/e/67e2dcf8777e4ef100fbc0532484f177db7d3483.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n+1} &gt; a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/a/86a17f53c2346cadc804f956eb15e919273c87cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n+2} = a_{n+1} - a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"135\" height=\"12\" />; then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/4/d94620bba29aad13418366ea8631019991e3bce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n+3} = a_{n+2} + a_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"150\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/7/e975077ed724116a41e91b38569d5933781337d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n+4} \\ge a_{n+3} - a_{n+2} = a_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"210\" height=\"16\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/8/6d815d2db043e5b070dc5d75b81dbea3b0f4e8e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_{n+2} = a_{n+4} + a_{n+3} + a_{n+2} \\ge (a_{n+1}) + (a_{n+2} + a_{n+1}) + a_{n+2} &gt; T_n + a_{n+2} \\ge T_n + m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"656\" height=\"18\" />.</li></ul>\n<p>Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/2/ca22d6e0b6b8ad9f0e9f53fc08a28f5a3477c3ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_{n+2k} &gt; T_n + mk$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"135\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/4/924308a4de890f9849585b4bc8e86570917789d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> is unbounded, as desired. \n</p><p><i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/A2&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/A2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><b>Comment by the proposer.</b>  The following statements are equivalent for a sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/6/5761114df6fcc5c1e89f4e685bab5a6ad24ecbe7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0, a_1, \\ldots, a_n, \\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"129\" height=\"11\" /> of real numbers satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/3/7b3cc10e9aafa734bad8d2df32a0242d47e461dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n = |a_{n+1} - a_{n+2}|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/c/e2c7d62172af0e738dd12f47f3f8ad8ef70cd65f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />: <br />\ni) the sequence is bounded; <br />\nii) the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> defined by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/7/fe7e8ab04feb6efe47fd192c7cf6cd073ee00f22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n,k) = a_na_k(a_n-a_k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"186\" height=\"18\" />, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/f/bcf02a4228c5c52cb3d09151b52f41be0b2a625d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n,k \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" />, is identically zero; <br />\niii) the sequence is of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/6/e96aa6c2fca9e5e5ebf63ce049c3b5e887c66981.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ldots, 0,a,a,0,a,a,0,a,a, \\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"209\" height=\"16\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/c/60c632dfe2dd9c8e9b2f677981b55d68f8e12610.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_IMO_Shortlist_Problems\" title=\"2004 IMO Shortlist Problems\">2004 IMO Shortlist Problems</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Germany_Pre-TST_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2005 Germany Pre-TST Problems (page does not exist)\">2005 Germany Pre-TST Problems</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_Romania_TST_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2005 Romania TST Problems (page does not exist)\">2005 Romania TST Problems</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?p=152740#p152740\">Discussion on AoPS/MathLinks</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?p=198930#198930\">Further discussion on AoPS/MathLinks</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017112458\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.048 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.064 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 602/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 353/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 22808/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.194      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n100.00%    6.194      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4985:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017112458 and revision id 28431. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}